# Normalise line endings on the way into the repository.
#
# Without this, six rule files ended up stored with CRLF while the rest of the
# corpus used LF -- invisible until a bulk edit rewrote them, at which point
# those six produced whole-file diffs that buried the actual change. Contributors
# on Windows will keep reintroducing it otherwise, because git's default
# core.autocrlf on that platform converts on checkout and back on commit only
# when it is configured to.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository for anything git detects as
# text, regardless of what the working tree uses. Editors on Windows handle LF
# fine; the tools in this repo read and write UTF-8 with explicit newline
# handling, so nothing here depends on CRLF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the file types this repo is made of, so the intent survives even
# if the wildcard above is ever narrowed.
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
